**Read:** [Petrology — Timothy Grove, MIT 12.109](../sources/MIT-Petrology-12-109.lingua#r_6Q1GZJKSZXQBM4N19CTRYG64TG), the complete tie-line, lever-rule, and ternary exercises; [Petrology — Stephen A. Nelson, Tulane EENS 2120](../sources/Petrology-Nelson-Tulane.lingua#r_1MNEKH4WW2GQRD4FZWNRD1GDPZ), the full corresponding phase-diagram notes; [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8), independent checks and conditioning in full.

For two coexisting phases α and β with component-B fractions x_α and x_β on the same basis, bulk x₀ = f_α x_α + f_β x_β and f_α+f_β = 1. If x_α < x₀ < x_β, f_β = (x₀−x_α)/(x_β−x_α). This is a balance, not a method for discovering the coexisting compositions without thermodynamic evidence.

For invented mole fractions x_α = 0.20, x_β = 0.80, and x₀ = 0.35, the phase mole fractions are f_α = 0.75 and f_β = 0.25. Check 0.75×0.20 + 0.25×0.80 = 0.35. Converting these to mass or volume requires the corresponding molar masses/densities and consistent phase definitions.

Near a vanishing tie-line gap, a fraction calculation can become sensitive to the input compositions. A bulk point outside the interval cannot be represented by two nonnegative fractions on that tie line. Negative phase amounts are a model/boundary diagnosis, not a geological result to round away.

**Work:** derive/check the example and solve a ternary three-phase balance, checking conservation and nonnegativity independently. Analyze sensitivity to the tie-line endpoints and distinguish uncertainty in those thermodynamic predictions from uncertainty in bulk composition. Follow [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8) for the shared numerical-validation step, whose mineralogy continuation leads to the original equilibrium example.

